  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "A = (2 −1 / 4 3) and B = (5 6 / −2 1). (a) Calculate A + B. (b) Calculate B − A."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Both matrices are 2 × 2, so you can add or subtract the numbers sitting in matching positions."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p195_q04.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p195-q04 from workbook page 195."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Confirm both matrices have the same order.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Both are 2 × 2, so addition and subtraction are allowed."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Conformable for + and −"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Add the entries in matching positions.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2 + 5 = 7; −1 + 6 = 5; 4 + (−2) = 2; 3 + 1 = 4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: A + B = (7 5 / 2 4)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Subtract each entry of A from the matching entry of B.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "5 − 2 = 3; 6 − (−1) = 7; −2 − 4 = −6; 1 − 3 = −2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: B − A = (3 7 / −6 −2)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Work position by position: top-left with top-left, top-right with top-right, and so on."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(a) A + B = (7 5 / 2 4)  (b) B − A = (3 7 / −6 −2)"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Matrix addition and subtraction are done element by element, so they are only defined when the two matrices have exactly the same order. Order matters for subtraction: B − A is the negative of A − B. Careful handling of the minus signs in 6 − (−1) is where most of the marks are won or lost."
    }
  ],
